  "family": "electronic",
  "lineage": "European computer-demo subculture music, formed on the Commodore Amiga after Karsten Obarski's Ultimate Soundtracker (1987) and carried onto PC by ProTracker, Scream Tracker, FastTracker II and Impulse Tracker — composed by Purple Motion, Skaven, Jesper Kyd, Lizardking and Necros for Future Crew, Triton and Renaissance demos and shown at Assembly and The Party — 120-165 BPM four-to-thirty-two-channel patterns of short looped samples entered as hexadecimal note tables, with heavy use of volume/pitch effect columns, sample offset tricks and slot-sharing to fake extra voices inside a few hundred kilobytes.",
